# Authentication

Auth strategy: `{{AUTH_STRATEGY}}`. Target URLs: `{{TARGET_URLS_JSON}}`. Runtime version: `{{AUTH_RUNTIME_VERSION}}`.

## Open-the-box behaviour

The generated CLI is self-contained: the first invocation runs
`scripts/install.sh`, which creates a local `.venv` and installs the only
external cookie dependency (`browser-cookie3`, PyPI/MIT). No manual `pip
install` is required.

## Providers

| Strategy | Order tried |
|---|---|
| `jd-internal` | `erp-sso-login` → browser jar via `browser-cookie3` |
| `browser-cookie` | browser jar only |
| `none` | *no cookie header attached* |

### Browser jar (universal fallback)

Reads cookies from the user's currently-signed-in browser (Edge / Chrome /
Firefox / Safari / Chromium / Brave / Opera / Vivaldi). Order can be
customised with `BROWSER_AUTH_BROWSERS=edge,chrome,firefox`.

If your OS decrypts Chrome cookies behind Keychain / DPAPI, the underlying
`browser-cookie3` library will handle the prompt / decryption on the first
call.

### `erp-sso-login` (京东内网优先)

Only relevant for JD internal targets (`*.jd.com`). The runtime auto-discovers
the skill in the following well-known locations before asking for a manual
override:

- `~/.claude/skills/erp-sso-login`
- `~/CodeSpace/claude-workspace/browser-forge-workspace/erp-sso-login`
- `~/browser-forge-workspace/erp-sso-login`
- `~/.oxygen/cli/erp-sso-login`
- `~/.local/share/erp-sso-login`

If the skill is installed elsewhere, export `ERP_SSO_LOGIN_HOME` to point at
its directory. 京ME 桌面客户端必须已登录。

## Overrides

- `BROWSER_FORGE_COOKIE_HEADER` — bypass discovery, use the given `Cookie:`
  header verbatim (for CI / one-off scripts).
- `BROWSER_FORGE_SKIP_AUTOINSTALL=1` — skip the first-run install (useful in
  restricted environments where you'll pre-install deps yourself).
- Command-level `--refresh-auth` — discard the in-process cache and force a
  fresh SSO / browser read on the next request.

## Never do this

- Never write a real `Cookie:` value into `manifest.json` or any repo file.
- Never log unredacted cookie values (the runtime's `RedactingFilter` strips
  them; keep it enabled).

## Diagnostics

```bash
scripts/{{ENTRYPOINT_NAME}} doctor      # provider availability + install.sh status
scripts/{{ENTRYPOINT_NAME}} auth-status # try to resolve, redacted summary
```
